This disk image contains the UAC system data file viewer "uac_view" and some data files extracted from my system. Copy the disk so the UAC directory isin the root of your working drive. From a shell with a PATH which includesthe UAC/CMDS directory type uac_view -w=/h0/uac/data then try a few options.This utility has a keyboard bindings file (.uacsrc) which can be editedto suit the terminal in use. It is searched for in the current data directory, /dd/sys, and /h0/sysP.E. 